# TestJavaToKotlinLangchain4j: langchain4j-core's main sources printed as Kotlin by maddi-cst-print-kotlin, without
# nullability verdicts, and judged by kotlinc 2.4.0 and by langchain4j-core's own tests (see JavaToKotlinRatchet's
# javadoc). Lower is better for printerCrashes and syntaxErrors, higher for syntaxCleanFiles, compilingFiles,
# bytecodeFiles and testBytecodeFiles (testsPassing and translatedTestsPassing are reported, not ratcheted, since
# 2026-10-12); `types` must not move.
# Write a better value here in the commit that earns it.
#
# 2026-10-09, first record, corpus at dab06ac18: 346 types; 1 printer crash (ImageContent: a duplicate key in the
# printer's map of Image); 345 files syntax-clean, 152 compiling against the original classes (588 type errors),
# 150 to class files. The tests (JUnit, Mockito, AssertJ): 1,111 pass on the original classes (5 skipped), 835 with
# the Kotlin classes in front; of 172 test files, 93 compile, and with those 823 pass.
# 2026-10-09, the import computer keeps one of two equal imports (ImageContent imports Image twice): no printer
# crash, 153 files compiling, 151 to class files.
# 2026-10-09, Java annotation types printed as annotation classes (the scanner keeps the elements' defaults), and
# a renamed String.formatted spreads its varargs: 233 files compiling (330 type errors), 229 to class files. The
# tests go DOWN, knowingly: 80 more Kotlin classes in front expose what a translation without verdicts gets wrong
# (non-null parameters handed null, lateinit properties never set, boxed parameters turned primitive in the JVM
# signature): 730 pass with the Kotlin classes; 85 test files compile against them, and with those 718 pass.
# 2026-10-10, Mockito matchers in translated tests wrapped so Kotlin does not check their null: 719 translated tests.
# 2026-10-10, a non-generic override of a generic member (AiServiceEvent.eventClass()/toBuilder()) printed with the
# member's type parameters and a cast: 249 files compiling (282 type errors), 245 to class files.
# 2026-10-10, annotation arguments (a Java annotation's array value spread, member annotation types named through their
# enclosing type), toArray(T[]), static references into mapped types, a raw Comparable, annotated parameters and primary
# constructors: 259 files compiling (242 type errors), 255 to class files, 90 test files compile.
# 2026-10-10, stream inference: a bound reference on nullable stream elements asserted in a lambda, a Collection<?>'s
# elements taken as Any?, explicit type arguments for type parameters only the result mentions (failures<Failure>()):
# 262 files compiling (228 type errors), 258 to class files, 94 test files compile.
# 2026-10-10, comparingDouble(map::get) asserted with its compared type, List::of over an array, qualified constructor
# references as lambdas, a translated annotation's value named where it is not the first element, a SAM constructor for
# a reference beside an overload taking T: 265 files compiling (214 type errors), 261 to class files; 765 tests pass
# with the Kotlin classes, 754 translated.
# 2026-10-12, the test counts are reported, not ratcheted (JavaToKotlinRatchet.TESTS): without verdicts every
# declaration prints non-null, and a class that newly compiles often fails its tests at runtime (a builder's unset
# lateinit property, a null into a non-null parameter), so a printer fix that gets more files compiling lowers them:
# this one from 765 to 685 with the Kotlin classes, 754 to 656 translated. maddi-mod's langchain4j-nullability
# ratchets them. No lateinit for a boxed or type-variable field, no fun interface for a generic method, a constructor
# that returns early kept secondary, a record whose accessor implements an interface's method printed without
# @JvmRecord, Java's char and byte promotions, a SAM constructor beside an overload taking another interface,
# Throwable's cause and message nullable, boxed types nullable in signatures Java calls, Integer.class as
# Int::class.javaObjectType, a read-only Object[] parameter as Array<out Any?>: 296 files compiling (135 type
# errors), 292 to class files.
# 2026-10-12, a constructor call takes the target's states beside a star, Java's Annotation is Kotlin's, an element
# out of a Collection<*> is an Any?, a cast keeps its own type variables: 300 files compiling (128 type errors), 297
# to class files.
types	346
printerCrashes	0
syntaxErrors	0
syntaxCleanFiles	346
compilingFiles	300
bytecodeFiles	297
testBytecodeFiles	94
